# Placeholder so this directory survives a clean clone.
#
# The only other thing that ever lives here is active-theme.conf, a
# symlink bin/bin/theme creates and .gitignore excludes — so without
# this file git has nothing to track here and the directory simply
# doesn't exist after `git clone`. bin/bin/theme's `ln -sfr` into a
# non-existent directory then fails silently (that script is
# deliberately `set -uo pipefail`, not -e, so one failed step doesn't
# abort the switch), and Qt apps get no theme at all with nothing
# logged anywhere. Existed on the original machine only because it was created
# by hand while Phase 5 was being built.
